<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<!--
	  Autheris collects nothing. There is no account, no analytics and no server of
	  ours: the tokens live in the Keychain on the device and the only network call
	  the app makes is the optional issuer-icon lookup (see the "Fetch issuer logos"
	  switch in Settings and the note in README.md).

	  The list below is therefore the one thing Apple actually requires of a
	  first-party app: a declaration of every "required reason" API it touches.
	  Both of the entries are real and are visible in the sources —

	  - UserDefaults (NSPrivacyAccessedAPICategoryUserDefaults, CA92.1): the app's own
	    preferences — the privacy switches, the accent theme, the sync flag, and the
	    `AppPreferences` blob `PreferencesStore` mirrors into the Keychain so they
	    survive a reinstall. The reason code CA92.1 is the one for "accessing
	    information from the same app, per its documentation". Nothing here is shared
	    with another app, which is what the code asserts.

	  - File timestamps (NSPrivacyAccessedAPICategoryFileTimestamp, C617.1): the
	    backup list reads each backup file's creation date to show and sort it
	    (`BackupView` and `OTPDataStore.listBackups`). Those files are the app's own,
	    inside its own container, which is the C617.1 reason.

	  If an API is added later — disk space, system boot time, active keyboards — it
	  needs an entry here and a reason code that matches how it is used. Apple's list
	  of codes is at https://developer.apple.com/documentation/bundleresources/privacy_manifest_files/describing_use_of_required_reason_api
	-->
	<key>NSPrivacyTracking</key>
	<false/>
	<key>NSPrivacyTrackingDomains</key>
	<array/>
	<key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypes</key>
	<array/>
	<key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPITypes</key>
	<array>
		<dict>
			<key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPIType</key>
			<string>NSPrivacyAccessedAPICategoryUserDefaults</string>
			<key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPITypeReasons</key>
			<array>
				<string>CA92.1</string>
			</array>
		</dict>
		<dict>
			<key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPIType</key>
			<string>NSPrivacyAccessedAPICategoryFileTimestamp</string>
			<key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPITypeReasons</key>
			<array>
				<string>C617.1</string>
			</array>
		</dict>
	</array>
</dict>
</plist>
